  journalLore: The old folk say a giant widow lays a hundred eggs under the roots, and that the ones you see are the ones that lived. They hunt where the big ones hunt, and they learn from them.
  journalAdvice: Smaller and quicker than the giant, with the same poison bite and pale web shot. A hammer cracks its shell; a blade can take its legs, and every leg it loses slows it.
